[23.992,"o","\r\n"]
[24.542,"o","\r\n GENERAL HEADINGS: P3.13 Fruit; P3.06 Soybeans; P3.11 Tobacco; J2A"]
[24.683,"o","\r\n Plant Production"]
[24.683,"o","\r\n"]
[25.15,"o","\r\n                     SPECIAL CLASSIFICATION AND HEADINGS"]
[25.675,"o","\r\n         S1015   Peaches                                   070%"]
[26.2,"o","\r\n         S2610   Flue-Cured Tobacco                        015%"]
[26.2,"o","\r\n"]
[26.65,"o","\r\n      BASIC 080%    APPLIED 020%    DEVELOPMENTAL 000%"]
[26.65,"o","\r\n"]
[27.208,"o","\r\n  OBJECTIVES:   To   develop   tissue  culture  and  gene  transfer"]
[27.758,"o","\r\n techniques  to  improve  disease  resistance and morphogenesis in"]
[28.308,"o","\r\n peach,  soybean,  and tobacco and to determine the role of ABA in"]
[28.692,"o","\r\n root morphogenesis of tissue-cultured plants."]
[28.692,"o","\r\n"]
[29.25,"o","\r\n  APPROACH: 1) Investigations with peach, soybean, and tobacco will"]
[29.8,"o","\r\n focus  on  transfer-  ring  genes via Agrobacterium-mediated gene"]
[30.35,"o","\r\n transfer and electroporation. DNA to be transferred will carry an"]
[30.9,"o","\r\n antibiotic  resistance  marker to permit selection of transformed"]
[31.45,"o","\r\n cells  prior to regeneration and either phytohor- mone-specifying"]
[32,"o","\r\n genes  calculated  to  overcome our inability to regenerate peach"]
[32.55,"o","\r\n and  soybean  plants from cell cultures that confer resistance to"]
[33.1,"o","\r\n several  bacterial  pathogens.  2) Investigations with peach will"]
[33.65,"o","\r\n also  include  testing the response of peach regenerants in vitro"]
[34.2,"o","\r\n and  under  greenhouse  conditions  to several peach pathogens as"]
[34.75,"o","\r\n well  as evaluating the field performance of peach plants derived"]
[35.3,"o","\r\n from  tissue  cultures.  Immunofluorescence,  GC/MS  and electron"]
[35.85,"o","\r\n microscopy  techniques  will  be used to study the role of ABA in"]
[36.4,"o","\r\n root  formation  of in vitro propagated peach shoots. Beltsville,"]
[36.95,"o","\r\n MD;  BG  006,  Room  1,  BL-1; RD-35; 06/10/91. Scientists: F. A."]
[37.2,"o","\r\n Hammerschlag and L. D. Owens."]
[37.2,"o","\r\n"]
[37.758,"o","\r\n  KEYWORDS:  GENE-TRANSFER  TISSUE-CULTURE PEACHES SOYBEANS TOBACCO"]
[38.308,"o","\r\n PLANT-IMPROVEMENT TREE-IMPROVEMENT CROP-PRODUCTION PLANT-GENETICS"]
[38.858,"o","\r\n GENETIC-ENGINEERING  PLANT-DISEASE-RESISTANCE MORPHOGENESIS ROOTS"]
[39.367,"o","\r\n ROOT-DEVELOPMENT AGROBACTERIUM ANTIBIOTIC-RESISTANCE MARKERS"]
[39.367,"o","\r\n"]
[39.567,"o","\r\n  PROGRESS: 8708 TO 9207"]
[40.117,"o","\r\n Field studies of tissue-cultured (TC), own-rooted peach cultivars"]
[40.667,"o","\r\n indicated thatTC trees produced significantly more fruit compared"]
[41.217,"o","\r\n with bud-grafted trees 2 and 3 years after planting in the field."]
[41.767,"o","\r\n These  studies  should  be  of  interest  to scientists and peach"]
[42.317,"o","\r\n growers   since   they   demonstrate  the  feasibility  of  using"]
[42.867,"o","\r\n TC-propagation  to  produce  own-rooted  peach  trees. Through in"]
[43.417,"o","\r\n vitro  selection  and  screening  for  somaclonal variants, peach"]
[43.967,"o","\r\n plants  have  been  obtained  with  stable  increased  levels  of"]
[44.517,"o","\r\n resistance  to  Xanthomonas  campestris pv. pruni and Pseudomonas"]
[45.067,"o","\r\n syringae  pv.  syringae.  These  studies should be of interest to"]
[45.617,"o","\r\n other  scientists concerned with improving woody crop species. An"]
[46.167,"o","\r\n in  vitro  screening  system  for  evaluating peach germplasm for"]
[46.717,"o","\r\n root-knot  nematode  resistance  was  developed that shortens the"]
[47.267,"o","\r\n screening period from 3 years to 5 weeks. This system can be used"]
[47.817,"o","\r\n to  evaluate  seedlings  and  peach  plants  derived  from tissue"]
[48.367,"o","\r\n culture      and      genetic     engineering     studies.     An"]
[48.917,"o","\r\n Agrobacterium-mediated  gene  transfer  system for peach has been"]
[49.467,"o","\r\n developed  for  peach  which  has  been  used  to  introduce  the"]
[50.017,"o","\r\n cytokinin  gene  into  peach  and  will  be used as the basis for"]
[50.567,"o","\r\n future   gene   transfer   studies.  A  gene  vector  pGT100  was"]
[51.117,"o","\r\n constructed   for   use   with  the  supervirulent  Agrobacterium"]
[51.667,"o","\r\n tumefaciens  helper  strain  EHA101.  pGT100/EHA101 proved highly"]
[52.217,"o","\r\n efficient  in  transferring  genes  to tobacco and soybean. These"]
[52.767,"o","\r\n studies  may  lead to improved methods for scientists to transfer"]
[53.142,"o","\r\n genes to these difficult to transform crops."]
[53.142,"o","\r\n"]
